  "implementation_roadmap": {
    "title": "Implementation Roadmap",
    "content": "The implementation roadmap for the AI Tutor for MBA Students is currently conceptual, heavily reliant on addressing critical knowledge gaps and validating core assumptions. The initial phase must focus on comprehensive market research to define the specific unmet learning needs, frequency, urgency, and willingness to pay among MBA students in the United States. This foundational research will inform product feature development and pedagogical approach.\n\nFollowing market validation, the next phase will involve defining the core product features, delivery model, and pedagogical approach, leading to the development of a minimum viable product (MVP). Concurrently, a robust business model, including pricing strategy and detailed cost structures, needs to be established and validated. This phase will also include exploring potential B2B partnerships with MBA programs or universities to gain legitimacy and distribution.\n\n The subsequent stages will focus on navigating the complex and evolving regulatory landscape for AI in US higher education, ensuring compliance with data privacy and academic integrity guidelines. A pilot program with a select group of MBA students will be crucial for gathering feedback, iterating on the product, and refining the go-to-market strategy before a broader launch. Success metrics will be defined based on the outcomes of the initial market research and pilot phases.",
