  "appendix": {
    "title": "Appendix",
    "content": "This appendix consolidates key unsupported claims and areas requiring further human review or validation, as identified throughout the proposal. These items represent critical uncertainties that directly impact the market opportunity, product definition, business model, and financial projections for the AI Tutor for MBA Students in the United States. Addressing these points is essential for developing a robust and evidence-backed business plan.\n\n**Unsupported Claims & Areas for Human Review**:\n*   The precise unmet learning needs, frequency, and urgency of MBA students requiring additional learning support. This impacts demand and potential revenue.\n*   The willingness of MBA students to pay for an AI tutor service. No pricing or willingness-to-pay data for MBA students is available.\n*   Specific product features, delivery model, pedagogical approach, integrations, and differentiation for the AI Tutor. These details directly impact development costs, value proposition, and pricing potential.\n*   Plausible commercial models, pricing, conversion rates, customer counts, costs, or margins for the AI Tutor. The business model has not been supplied, and no financial data is available.\n*   The specific market size for AI tutors targeting MBA students in the United States. While the general US AI education market size is provided, it is not segmented for higher education or MBA students specifically.\n*   Information regarding the legal position of such a service or potential institutional partnerships with MBA programs. This impacts potential revenue streams and compliance costs.\n*   Strategy for addressing the low perception of AI benefits in education among the US public and the low adoption rate among higher education faculty.\n*   Guidance on navigating the complex and evolving regulatory landscape for AI in US higher education, particularly concerning data privacy and academic integrity.\n\n**Source Notes**:\n*   web-57da4247bdb54dd99b32029fe64